IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulation 36: ALLOCATION OF EARNINGS FOR BENEFIT PURPOSES.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt (consolidation current to 2026-09-30); nothing here is claimed to be verified against the
-- official text.
--
-- HOW IT IS BUILT. Reg 36 decides, for earnings already determined under reg 35, WHICH WEEKS they are put on,
-- and in a few subsections HOW MUCH goes on each week.
--   * "Which weeks" is a manner (`er3 Manner of allocation`), one constructor per distinct outcome. Each
--     subsection that picks a manner is its own rule over the list of facts that hold of the earnings
--     (`er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`), and answers JUST the manner when it applies and NOTHING
--     when it does not. `reg 36 the manners of allocation that apply` collects them in the order given at
--     that rule. The text states no priority among subsections that can overlap (fork F3).
--   * "How much" is arithmetic that the text spells out: the proportion of (3), the transaction shares of
--     (6.1), the weekly spread of (8), (9), (10), (11) and (15), the annuity of (17). Amounts are dollars
--     (NUMBERs); a week is the DATE of its Sunday; a fraction of a dollar is rounded as (20) says.
--   * A judgment the text leaves to the Commission (a referral under s 25(1)(a); the conditions for ending a
--     referral under s 27(1.1)(b)) is an input.
-- Out of range: the maximum yearly insurable earnings of s 4 (piece ei-g0 gives the formula, the published
-- figure is an input), the survival probabilities and bond yield of (17) (published outside the texts).

§ `The manners of allocation and the facts they turn on`

-- The outcome of the subsections that say to which weeks earnings are put. One constructor per distinct
-- outcome; the comment names the subsections that give it.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(2) to (19) (src:609-666)
DECLARE `er3 Manner of allocation` IS ONE OF
    `er3 manner: not allocated to any week`                                                             -- (2)
    `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`                                    -- (4), (19)(a)
    `er3 manner: to the period for which the earnings are payable`                                      -- (5), (18)
    `er3 manner: to the weeks in which the services were performed`                                     -- (6)
    `er3 manner: by the transaction rule of subsection (6.1)`                                           -- (6.1), (7)(a)
    `er3 manner: equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned`      -- (6.2)
    `er3 manner: to the week in which the subsidy was paid`                                             -- (7)(b)
    `er3 manner: vacation pay for a specific vacation period, made up to normal weekly earnings`        -- (8)(a)
    `er3 manner: vacation pay in any other case, at normal weekly earnings for each week but the last`  -- (8)(b)
    `er3 manner: earnings by reason of a lay-off or separation, at normal weekly earnings from the week of the lay-off or separation` -- (9), (10)
    `er3 manner: an award or settlement for specific weeks, at normal weekly earnings from the first week awarded` -- (11)
    `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`                     -- (12)
    `er3 manner: to the week in which the holiday or non-working day occurs`                            -- (13)
    `er3 manner: periodic pension moneys, to the period for which they are paid or payable`             -- (14)
    `er3 manner: lump-sum pension moneys, at the weekly annuity amount from the first week`             -- (15)
    `er3 manner: to the week in which the transaction occurs`                                           -- (19)(b)

-- The facts a witness could state about earnings that are to be allocated. A fact not on the list does
-- not hold. Each is named for what the subsection says.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(2) to (19) (src:609-666)
DECLARE `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated` IS ONE OF
    `er3 earnings: they did not constitute earnings, or were not taken into account as earnings, under section 35` -- (2)
    `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment for the performance of services`              -- (4)
    `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment without the performance of services`          -- (5)
    `er3 earnings: payable by an employer in consideration of the claimant returning to or beginning work` -- (5)
    `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed`                                                       -- (6), (6.1), (6.2), (7)
    `er3 earnings: from participation in profits or commissions`                                        -- (6), (6.1), (6.2)
    `er3 earnings: they arise from the performance of services`                                        -- (6), (19)(a)
    `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction`                                                       -- (6.1), (7)(a), (19)(b)
    `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed in farming`                                            -- (7)
    `er3 earnings: received in the form of a subsidy`                                                   -- (7)(b)
    `er3 earnings: vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation`        -- (8)
    `er3 earnings: the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods`       -- (8)(a)
    `er3 earnings: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment`             -- (9)
    `er3 earnings: paid or payable under a labour arbitration award or tribunal judgment, or as a settlement of an issue that might have been so determined` -- (11)
    `er3 earnings: awarded in respect of specific weeks as a result of a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted` -- (11)
    `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children` -- (12)(a)
    `er3 earnings: a payment under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan`             -- (12)(b)
    `er3 earnings: a payment referred to in paragraph 35(2)(d) or (f)`                                  -- (12)(c)
    `er3 earnings: workers' compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement` -- (12)(d)
    `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a family member`                      -- (12)(e)
    `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child`               -- (12)(f)
    `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult`               -- (12)(g)
    `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day observed as such by law, custom or agreement` -- (13)
    `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day immediately preceding or following one that occurs at the establishment of the employer or former employer` -- (13)
    `er3 earnings: the moneys referred to in paragraph 35(2)(e)`                                        -- (14), (15)
    `er3 earnings: paid or payable on a periodic basis`                                                 -- (14)
    `er3 earnings: paid or payable in a lump sum`                                                       -- (15)
    `er3 earnings: payable under a government program intended to encourage re-employment, as a supplement to earnings arising from a contract of employment` -- (18)

GIVEN fact IS AN `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
      facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` fact facts MEANS elem fact facts

§ `Section 36(20) -- rounding`

-- src:667 | (20) For the purposes of this section, a fraction of a dollar that is equal to or greater than one half shall be taken as a dollar and a fraction that is less than one half shall be disregarded.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(20) (src:667)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` IS FLOOR (amount PLUS 0.5)

§ `Sections 36(1), 36(2) -- what is allocated`

-- src:608 | 36 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the earnings of a claimant as determined under section 35 shall be allocated to weeks in the manner described in this section and, for the purposes referred to in subsection 35(2), shall be the earnings of the claimant for those weeks.
-- src:609 | (2) For the purposes of this section, the earnings of a claimant shall not be allocated to weeks during which they did not constitute earnings or were not taken into account as earnings under section 35.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(1), (2) (src:608-609)
GIVEN `the income is earnings determined under section 35` IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(1) and (2) the earnings are allocated to weeks` IF
        `the income is earnings determined under section 35`
    AND NOT (`reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they did not constitute earnings, or were not taken into account as earnings, under section 35` facts)

§ `Section 36(3) -- a period that does not coincide with a week`

-- A week is the DATE of its Sunday; it runs from that Sunday to the Saturday six days later.
-- src:610 | (3) Where the period for which earnings of a claimant are payable does not coincide with a week, the earnings shall be allocated to any week that is wholly or partly in the period in the proportion that the number of days worked in the week bears to the number of days worked in the period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(3) (src:610)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of days`
      week IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` IF
        week AT MOST period's `last day of the period`
    AND (`s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` week) AT LEAST period's `first day of the period`

-- src:610 | (3) Where the period for which earnings of a claimant are payable does not coincide with a week, the earnings shall be allocated to any week that is wholly or partly in the period in the proportion that the number of days worked in the week bears to the number of days worked in the period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(3) (src:610)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(3) the period does not coincide with a week` IF
    NOT (    period's `first day of the period` EQUALS `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` (period's `first day of the period`)
         AND period's `last day of the period` EQUALS `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (period's `first day of the period`))

-- The earnings go on any week wholly or partly in the period in the proportion that the days worked in the
-- week bear to the days worked in the period, rounded as (20) says. Where (3) does not apply (the period
-- coincides with a week) or no day was worked in the period, the case is not covered: NOTHING.
-- src:610 | (3) Where the period for which earnings of a claimant are payable does not coincide with a week, the earnings shall be allocated to any week that is wholly or partly in the period in the proportion that the number of days worked in the week bears to the number of days worked in the period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(3) (src:610)
GIVEN `the earnings payable for the period` IS A NUMBER
      period IS A `Period of days`
      week IS A DATE
      `the days worked in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the days worked in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` IS
    IF (NOT (`reg 36(3) the period does not coincide with a week` period)) OR `the days worked in the period` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `reg 36(3) the week is wholly or partly in the period` period week
         THEN JUST (`reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` ((`the earnings payable for the period` TIMES `the days worked in the week`) DIVIDED BY `the days worked in the period`))
         ELSE JUST 0

§ `Sections 36(4) to 36(7) -- the manner for earnings from services, transactions and profits`

-- src:611 | (4) Earnings that are payable to a claimant under a contract of employment for the performance of services shall be allocated to the period in which the services were performed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(4) (src:611)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(4) earnings payable under a contract of employment for the performance of services` IS
    IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment for the performance of services` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:612 | (5) Earnings that are payable to a claimant under a contract of employment without the performance of services or payable by an employer to a claimant in consideration of the claimant returning to or beginning work shall be allocated to the period for which they are payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(5) (src:612)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(5) earnings payable without the performance of services or to induce a return to or the beginning of work` IS
    IF    `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment without the performance of services` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: payable by an employer in consideration of the claimant returning to or beginning work` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the period for which the earnings are payable`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (6), (6.1) and (6.2) are about "the earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a
-- claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions".
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36 the earnings are of a self-employed claimant or from profits or commissions` IF
       `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed` facts
    OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: from participation in profits or commissions` facts

-- src:613 | (6) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that arise from the performance of services shall be allocated to the weeks in which those services are performed.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6) (src:613)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(6) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from the performance of services` IS
    IF    `reg 36 the earnings are of a self-employed claimant or from profits or commissions` facts
       AND `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from the performance of services` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in which the services were performed`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:614 | (6.1) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that arise from a transaction shall be allocated
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6.1) (src:614)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(6.1) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from a transaction` IS
    IF    `reg 36 the earnings are of a self-employed claimant or from profits or commissions` facts
       AND `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: by the transaction rule of subsection (6.1)`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:617 | (6.2) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that do not arise from the performance of services or from a transaction shall be allocated equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6.2) (src:617)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(6.2) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from neither services nor a transaction` IS
    IF    `reg 36 the earnings are of a self-employed claimant or from profits or commissions` facts
       AND NOT (`reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from the performance of services` facts)
       AND NOT (`reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction` facts)
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7) A claimant self-employed in farming: (a) earnings from a transaction go by (6.1); (b) earnings received
-- as a subsidy go to the week in which the subsidy was paid.
-- src:618 | (7) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed in farming shall be allocated
-- src:619 | (a) if they arose from a transaction, in accordance with subsection (6.1); and
-- src:620 | (b) if they were received in the form of a subsidy, to the week in which the subsidy was paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(7) (src:618-620)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(7) earnings of a claimant who is self-employed in farming` IS
    IF NOT (`reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed in farming` facts)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction` facts
         THEN JUST `er3 manner: by the transaction rule of subsection (6.1)`
         ELSE IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: received in the form of a subsidy` facts
              THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the week in which the subsidy was paid`
              ELSE NOTHING

-- The week in which a day falls, by the DATE of its Sunday: the week of the subsidy's payment (7)(b), of the
-- holiday (13), of the transaction (19)(b).
-- src:620 | (b) if they were received in the form of a subsidy, to the week in which the subsidy was paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(7)(b) (src:620)
GIVEN `the day on which the subsidy was paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 36(7)(b) the week to which a farming subsidy is allocated` IS
    `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the subsidy was paid`

§ `Section 36(6.1) -- earnings from a transaction`

-- The weekly threshold: "the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided
-- by 52". The yearly figure is an input (s 4 gives the formula; the published figure is not in the texts).
-- src:614 | (6.1) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that arise from a transaction shall be allocated
-- src:615 | (a) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the weeks in which the work that gave rise to the transaction was performed, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks or, if no such work was performed, to the week in which the transaction occurred; or
-- src:616 | (b) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is less than or equal to the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the week in which the transaction occurred or, if the claimant demonstrates that the work that gave rise to the transaction occurred in more than one week, to the weeks in which the earnings were earned, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6.1) (src:614-616)
GIVEN `the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(6.1)(a) the aggregate is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52` IF
    `the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week` GREATER THAN (`the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act` DIVIDED BY 52)

-- Where the manner is by the transaction rule:
-- (a) greater than the threshold: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work
--     performed in each, or, if no such work was performed, to the week in which the transaction occurred;
-- (b) at most the threshold: to the week in which the transaction occurred or, if the claimant demonstrates
--     that the work occurred in more than one week, to the weeks in which the earnings were earned, in
--     proportion to the work performed in each.
DECLARE `er3 Allocation of earnings from a transaction` IS ONE OF
    `er3 transaction: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work performed in each week`
    `er3 transaction: to the week in which the transaction occurred`

-- src:614 | (6.1) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that arise from a transaction shall be allocated
-- src:615 | (a) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the weeks in which the work that gave rise to the transaction was performed, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks or, if no such work was performed, to the week in which the transaction occurred; or
-- src:616 | (b) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is less than or equal to the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the week in which the transaction occurred or, if the claimant demonstrates that the work that gave rise to the transaction occurred in more than one week, to the weeks in which the earnings were earned, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6.1)(a), (b) (src:614-616)
GIVEN `the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `work that gave rise to the transaction was performed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant demonstrates that the work that gave rise to the transaction occurred in more than one week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er3 Allocation of earnings from a transaction`
DECIDE `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` IS
    IF `reg 36(6.1)(a) the aggregate is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52` `the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act`
    THEN (IF `work that gave rise to the transaction was performed`
          THEN `er3 transaction: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work performed in each week`
          ELSE `er3 transaction: to the week in which the transaction occurred`)
    ELSE (IF `the claimant demonstrates that the work that gave rise to the transaction occurred in more than one week`
          THEN `er3 transaction: to the weeks in which the work was performed, in proportion to the work performed in each week`
          ELSE `er3 transaction: to the week in which the transaction occurred`)

-- The share of the earnings that goes on one week when they go to the weeks of the work in proportion to the
-- work performed in each, rounded as (20) says. No work at all: not covered, NOTHING.
-- src:615 | (a) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the weeks in which the work that gave rise to the transaction was performed, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks or, if no such work was performed, to the week in which the transaction occurred; or
-- src:616 | (b) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is less than or equal to the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the week in which the transaction occurred or, if the claimant demonstrates that the work that gave rise to the transaction occurred in more than one week, to the weeks in which the earnings were earned, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6.1)(a), (b) (src:615-616)
GIVEN `the earnings from the transaction` IS A NUMBER
      `the work performed in the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the work performed in all the weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(6.1) the share of the earnings allocated to a week in proportion to the work` IS
    IF `the work performed in all the weeks` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` ((`the earnings from the transaction` TIMES `the work performed in the week`) DIVIDED BY `the work performed in all the weeks`))

-- (6.2) Equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned. Which weeks "fall
-- within" a period is not settled by the text (fork F4): the number of weeks is an input.
-- src:617 | (6.2) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that do not arise from the performance of services or from a transaction shall be allocated equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(6.2) (src:617)
GIVEN `the earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks falling within the period in which the earnings were earned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(6.2) the equal share allocated to each week` IS
    IF `the number of weeks falling within the period in which the earnings were earned` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the earnings` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks falling within the period in which the earnings were earned`))

§ `The spreading of an amount at normal weekly earnings -- shared by (8), (9), (10), (11) and (15)`

-- Subsections (8)(a), (8)(b), (9), (11) and (15) each spread an amount over consecutive weeks so that each
-- week but the last holds a stated weekly amount. This is their shared arithmetic, not a provision of the text.
-- (8)(a), (9) and (11) say the claimant's TOTAL earnings from the employment in each week are the normal
-- weekly earnings, so what is put on a week is the normal weekly earnings less the other earnings from the
-- same employment on that week; (8)(b) and (15) say the amount put on each week is the stated amount itself,
-- which is this spread with no other earnings. `others` is the other earnings of the first week, the second
-- week and so on; a week beyond the list has none.
GIVEN remaining IS A NUMBER
      weekly IS A NUMBER
      other IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 36 the amount of what remains that fits on a week` remaining weekly other MEANS
    min remaining (max 0 (weekly MINUS other))

GIVEN remaining IS A NUMBER
      weekly IS A NUMBER
      others IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` IS
    IF remaining AT MOST 0 OR weekly AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE CONSIDER others
         WHEN EMPTY THEN
             (`reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`reg 36 the amount of what remains that fits on a week` remaining weekly 0))
                 FOLLOWED BY `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` (remaining MINUS (`reg 36 the amount of what remains that fits on a week` remaining weekly 0)) weekly EMPTY
         WHEN o FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
             (`reg 36(20) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`reg 36 the amount of what remains that fits on a week` remaining weekly o))
                 FOLLOWED BY `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` (remaining MINUS (`reg 36 the amount of what remains that fits on a week` remaining weekly o)) weekly rest

§ `Section 36(8) -- vacation pay`

-- (8)(a) For a specific vacation period or periods: put on the weeks that begin with the first week and end not
-- later than the last week of the vacation period(s), so that the claimant's total earnings from the
-- employment are the normal weekly earnings in each consecutive week. `others` is the other earnings from the
-- employment on each week of the vacation period(s), in order; the amounts are those of the same weeks.
-- src:621 | (8) Where vacation pay is paid or payable to a claimant for a reason other than a lay-off or separation from an employment, it shall be allocated as follows:
-- src:622 | (a) where the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods, it shall be allocated
-- src:623 | (i) to a number of weeks that begins with the first week and ends not later than the last week of the vacation period or periods, and
-- src:624 | (ii) in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each consecutive week, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(8)(a) (src:621-624)
GIVEN `the vacation pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation period or periods` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(8)(a) the amounts put on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` IS
    take (count `the other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation period or periods`)
         (`reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` `the vacation pay` `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation period or periods`)

-- (8)(a) The text puts the pay on weeks that end "not later than the last week of the vacation period or
-- periods"; it does not say where pay goes that does not fit in those weeks (fork F5). This is that excess.
-- src:621 | (8) Where vacation pay is paid or payable to a claimant for a reason other than a lay-off or separation from an employment, it shall be allocated as follows:
-- src:622 | (a) where the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods, it shall be allocated
-- src:623 | (i) to a number of weeks that begins with the first week and ends not later than the last week of the vacation period or periods, and
-- src:624 | (ii) in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each consecutive week, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(8)(a) (src:621-624)
GIVEN `the vacation pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation period or periods` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(8)(a) the vacation pay that does not fit on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` IS
    `the vacation pay` MINUS (sum (`reg 36(8)(a) the amounts put on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` `the vacation pay` `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation period or periods`))

-- (8)(b) In any other case: when paid, on the weeks that begin with the first week for which it is payable,
-- the amount put on each week but the last being the normal weekly earnings.
-- src:625 | (b) in any other case, the vacation pay shall, when paid, be allocated
-- src:626 | (i) to a number of weeks that begins with the first week for which it is payable, and
-- src:627 | (ii) in such a manner that, for each week except the last, the amount allocated under this subsection is equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(8)(b) (src:625-627)
GIVEN `the vacation pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` IS
    `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` `the vacation pay` `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` EMPTY

-- src:621 | (8) Where vacation pay is paid or payable to a claimant for a reason other than a lay-off or separation from an employment, it shall be allocated as follows:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(8) (src:621)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(8) vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation` IS
    IF NOT (`reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation` facts)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods` facts
         THEN JUST `er3 manner: vacation pay for a specific vacation period, made up to normal weekly earnings`
         ELSE JUST `er3 manner: vacation pay in any other case, at normal weekly earnings for each week but the last`

§ `Sections 36(9) to 36(11) -- earnings by reason of a lay-off or separation, and awards`

-- src:628 | (9) Subject to subsections (10) to (11), all earnings paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment shall, regardless of the period in respect of which the earnings are purported to be paid or payable, be allocated to a number of weeks that begins with the week of the lay-off or separation in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each consecutive week except the last, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(9) (src:628)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(9) earnings paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment` IS
    IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: earnings by reason of a lay-off or separation, at normal weekly earnings from the week of the lay-off or separation`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (9) The amounts on the consecutive weeks that begin with the week of the lay-off or separation: the
-- claimant's total earnings from the employment are the normal weekly earnings in each week but the last.
-- `others` is the other earnings from the same employment on that week, the next and so on.
-- src:628 | (9) Subject to subsections (10) to (11), all earnings paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment shall, regardless of the period in respect of which the earnings are purported to be paid or payable, be allocated to a number of weeks that begins with the week of the lay-off or separation in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each consecutive week except the last, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(9) (src:628)
GIVEN `the earnings paid or payable by reason of the lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(9) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` IS
    `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` `the earnings paid or payable by reason of the lay-off or separation` `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation`

-- (10) Later earnings by reason of the same lay-off or separation are added to the earnings already allocated
-- and the allocation is made again on the total.
-- src:629 | (10) Subject to subsection (11), where earnings are paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment subsequent to an allocation under subsection (9) in respect of that lay-off or separation, the subsequent earnings shall be added to the earnings that were allocated and, regardless of the period in respect of which the subsequent earnings are purported to be paid or payable, a revised allocation shall be made in accordance with subsection (9) on the basis of that total.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(10) (src:629)
GIVEN `the earnings already allocated under subsection (9)` IS A NUMBER
      `the subsequent earnings paid or payable by reason of the same lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(10) the revised amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` IS
    `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` (`the earnings already allocated under subsection (9)` PLUS `the subsequent earnings paid or payable by reason of the same lay-off or separation`) `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation`

-- (11) Earnings awarded for specific weeks by a labour arbitration award, a tribunal's judgment or a settlement
-- following a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted: on consecutive weeks beginning
-- with the first week awarded, so that the total from the employment is the normal weekly earnings in each
-- week but the last.
-- src:640 | (11) Where earnings are paid or payable in respect of an employment pursuant to a labour arbitration award or the judgment of a tribunal, or as a settlement of an issue that might otherwise have been determined by a labour arbitration award or the judgment of a tribunal, and the earnings are awarded in respect of specific weeks as a result of a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted, the earnings shall be allocated to a number of consecutive weeks, beginning with the first week in respect of which the earnings are awarded, in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each week except the last week, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(11) (src:640)
