§ `Sections 36(10.1), 36(10.2) -- when the lay-off allocation does not apply`

-- (10.1) The allocation of (9) does not apply if all four of (a) to (d) hold. Dates are data:
-- (a) a benefit period that begins from January 25, 2009 to May 29, 2010, both ends included.
-- (b) at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium paid in at least seven of the 10 years before.
-- (c) fewer than 36 weeks of regular benefits paid in the 260 weeks before.
-- (d) a referral under s 25(1)(a) of the Act, during the allocation period or (if five weeks or fewer) within
--     six weeks after the notification of the allocation, to a course that is full-time, lasts at least 10
--     weeks or costs at least $5,000 or at least 80% of the lay-off earnings, is wholly paid for by the
--     claimant, and begins during one of the 52 weeks following the beginning of the benefit period.
-- "at least $5,000 or 80%": either threshold suffices (fork F6); "during one of the 52 weeks following the
-- beginning of the benefit period" is read as after that day and no later than 52 weeks (364 days) after it
-- (fork F7). Out of range: s 25(1)(a) of the Act (piece ei2), the referral being the Commission's act.
-- src:631 | (a) the claimant’s benefit period begins in the period beginning on January 25, 2009 and ending on May 29, 2010;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(10.1)(a) (src:631)
GIVEN `the first day of the claimant's benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(10.1)(a) the benefit period begins from January 25, 2009 to May 29, 2010` IF
        `the first day of the claimant's benefit period` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25)
    AND `the first day of the claimant's benefit period` AT MOST (YearMonthDay 2010 5 29)

-- src:636 | (ii) that has a duration of at least 10 weeks or that costs at least $5,000 or 80% of the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant’s lay-off or separation from employment,
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(10.1)(d)(ii) (src:636)
GIVEN `the course or program lasts this many weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the course or program costs this many dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant's lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(10.1)(d)(ii) the course lasts at least 10 weeks or costs at least $5,000 or 80% of the earnings` IF
       `the course or program lasts this many weeks` AT LEAST 10
    OR `the course or program costs this many dollars` AT LEAST 5000
    OR `the course or program costs this many dollars` AT LEAST (80% TIMES `the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant's lay-off or separation`)

-- src:630 | (10.1) The allocation of the earnings paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment made in accordance with subsection (9) does not apply if
-- src:631 | (a) the claimant’s benefit period begins in the period beginning on January 25, 2009 and ending on May 29, 2010;
-- src:632 | (b) the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in at least seven of the 10 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:633 | (c) the Commission paid the claimant less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period; and
-- src:634 | (d) during the period in which the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant’s lay-off or separation from an employment are allocated in accordance with subsection (9) or, if the earnings are allocated to five weeks or less, during that period of allocation or within six weeks following the notification of the allocation, the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training
-- src:635 | (i) that is full-time,
-- src:636 | (ii) that has a duration of at least 10 weeks or that costs at least $5,000 or 80% of the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant’s lay-off or separation from employment,
-- src:637 | (iii) for which the claimant assumes the entire cost, and
-- src:638 | (iv) that begins during one of the 52 weeks following the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(10.1) (src:630-638)
GIVEN `the first day of the claimant's benefit period` IS A DATE
      `the number of the 10 years before the beginning of the benefit period in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of regular benefits the Commission paid the claimant in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `the allocation period of the earnings paid or payable by reason of the lay-off or separation` IS A `Period of days`
      `the day on which the claimant was notified of the allocation` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority it designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training` IS A DATE
      `the course or program is full-time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the course or program lasts this many weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the course or program costs this many dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant's lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant assumes the entire cost of the course or program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the course or program begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(10.1) the allocation under subsection (9) does not apply` IF
        -- (a)
        `reg 36(10.1)(a) the benefit period begins from January 25, 2009 to May 29, 2010` `the first day of the claimant's benefit period`
        -- (b)
    AND `the number of the 10 years before the beginning of the benefit period in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium` AT LEAST 7
        -- (c)
    AND `the weeks of regular benefits the Commission paid the claimant in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the benefit period` LESS THAN 36
        -- (d) the referral, within the window the paragraph gives
    AND `reg 36(10.1)(d) the referral is within the window of the allocation` `the allocation period of the earnings paid or payable by reason of the lay-off or separation` `the day on which the claimant was notified of the allocation` `the day on which the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority it designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training`
        -- (d)(i) to (iv) the course
    AND `the course or program is full-time`
    AND `reg 36(10.1)(d)(ii) the course lasts at least 10 weeks or costs at least $5,000 or 80% of the earnings` `the course or program lasts this many weeks` `the course or program costs this many dollars` `the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant's lay-off or separation`
    AND `the claimant assumes the entire cost of the course or program`
    AND `the day on which the course or program begins` GREATER THAN `the first day of the claimant's benefit period`
    AND `the day on which the course or program begins` AT MOST (`the first day of the claimant's benefit period` PLUS (`weeks as days` 52))

-- The window of (d): the referral falls during the period in which the earnings are allocated, or, if they
-- are allocated to five weeks or fewer, during that period or within six weeks after the notification.
-- src:634 | (d) during the period in which the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant’s lay-off or separation from an employment are allocated in accordance with subsection (9) or, if the earnings are allocated to five weeks or less, during that period of allocation or within six weeks following the notification of the allocation, the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(10.1)(d) (src:634)
GIVEN allocated IS A `Period of days`
      `the day on which the claimant was notified of the allocation` IS A DATE
      referral IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(10.1)(d) the referral is within the window of the allocation` IF
        `the day` referral `falls within` allocated
    OR (    (`the number of days in` allocated) AT MOST (`weeks as days` 5)
        AND referral GREATER THAN `the day on which the claimant was notified of the allocation`
        AND referral AT MOST (`the day on which the claimant was notified of the allocation` PLUS (`weeks as days` 6)))

-- (10.2) If any condition under which the Commission may end the referral under s 27(1.1)(b) of the Act
-- exists, the earnings are allocated again under (9). The existence of such a condition is an input
-- (out of range: s 27(1.1)(b), piece ei2).
-- src:639 | (10.2) If any of the conditions under which the Commission may terminate the claimant’s referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists, the earnings paid or payable to the claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment shall be re-allocated under subsection (9).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(10.2) (src:639)
GIVEN `the allocation under subsection (9) does not apply by reason of subsection (10.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a condition under which the Commission may terminate the claimant's referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 36(9) the earnings are allocated under subsection (9), after subsections (10.1) and (10.2)` IF
        NOT (`the allocation under subsection (9) does not apply by reason of subsection (10.1)`)
    OR `a condition under which the Commission may terminate the claimant's referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists`

§ `Sections 36(12) to 36(19) -- the remaining kinds of earnings`

-- (12) The seven kinds of payment that go to the weeks in respect of which they are paid or payable.
-- src:641 | (12) The following payments shall be allocated to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable:
-- src:642 | (a) payments in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act;
-- src:643 | (b) payments under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan;
-- src:644 | (c) payments referred to in paragraphs 35(2)(d) and (f);
-- src:645 | (d) workers’ compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers’ compensation payments;
-- src:646 | (e) payments in respect of the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act;
-- src:647 | (f) payments in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child; and
-- src:648 | (g) payments in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(12) (src:641-648)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(12) payments allocated to the weeks in respect of which they are paid or payable` IS
    IF    `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: a payment under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: a payment referred to in paragraph 35(2)(d) or (f)` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: workers' compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a family member` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child` facts
       OR `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (13) A payment for a holiday or non-working day (observed by law, custom or agreement), or for one next
-- to a holiday or non-working day at the employer's establishment, goes to the week in which that day occurs.
