    `reg 36 the amounts put on consecutive weeks` `the lump sum` `the weekly amount calculated in accordance with subsection (17)` EMPTY

-- (16) The moneys allocated under (14) or (15) are not taken into account in allocating other earnings: of the
-- earnings already on a week, those allocated under (14) or (15) are left out. The pair is the amount and
-- whether it was allocated under (14) or (15).
-- src:652 | (16) The moneys allocated in accordance with subsection (14) or (15) shall not be taken into account in the allocation of other earnings under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(16) (src:652)
DECLARE `er3 Earnings already on a week` HAS
    amount IS A NUMBER
    `allocated under subsection (14) or (15)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:652 | (16) The moneys allocated in accordance with subsection (14) or (15) shall not be taken into account in the allocation of other earnings under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(16) (src:652)
GIVEN earnings IS A LIST OF `er3 Earnings already on a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(16) the earnings taken into account in allocating other earnings` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN e YIELD e's amount)
             (filter (GIVEN e YIELD NOT (e's `allocated under subsection (14) or (15)`)) earnings))

-- (17) The weekly amount is A divided by B, A being the lump sum and B the estimated actuarial present value
-- of $1 payable at the beginning of every week for the claimant's lifetime from the day the lump sum is paid
-- or payable: B = [ sum over t of (tPx / (1 + i)^t) - 0.5 ] x 52. tPx is the probability that the claimant,
-- aged x on that day, survives t years (the latest Canadian mortality rates used in the valuation of the
-- Canada Pension Plan, prorated equally between males and females); i is the annualized long-term Government
-- of Canada benchmark bond yield averaged over the 12 months from September 1 to August 30 before the
-- January 1 on which the values take effect, as a percentage rounded to the nearest one tenth of a
-- percentage. Neither the rates nor the yield is in the texts: the probabilities (for t = 0, 1, 2, ...) and
-- the yield are inputs. The text sums to infinity; only the supplied terms are summed (fork F8).
-- src:653 | (17) The weekly amount shall be calculated in accordance with the following formula, according to the claimant’s age on the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable:
-- src:654 | A / B
-- src:655 | where
-- src:656 | A is the lump sum payment; and
-- src:657 | B is the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week starting from the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable and payable for the claimant’s lifetime, as calculated each year in accordance with the following formula and effective on January 1 of the year following its calculation:
-- src:658 | B = [Σt = 0 to infinity of (tPx/ (1+ i)t) – 0.5] × 52
-- src:659 | where
-- src:660 | tPx is the probability that the claimant will survive for “t” years from the claimant’s age “x” using the latest Canadian mortality rates used in the valuation of the Canada Pension Plan prorated in equal parts between males and females,
-- src:661 | i is the annualized long-term Government of Canada benchmark bond yields averaged over the 12-month period beginning on the September 1 and ending on the August 30 before the January 1 on which the estimated actuarial present values are effective, expressed as a percentage and rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage, and
-- src:662 | t is the number of years that the claimant survives according to the claimant’s age for which the probablity of survival is estimated by tPx.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(17) (src:653-662)
GIVEN yield IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(17) the yield i rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage` IS
    (FLOOR ((yield TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 1000

GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(17) one plus the yield to the power of the number of years` IS
    IF years AT MOST 0 THEN 1 ELSE base TIMES (`reg 36(17) one plus the yield to the power of the number of years` base (years MINUS 1))

GIVEN survival IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      yield IS A NUMBER
      t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(17) the sum of tPx / (1 + i)^t from year t on` IS
    CONSIDER survival
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (p DIVIDED BY (`reg 36(17) one plus the yield to the power of the number of years` (1 PLUS yield) t))
            PLUS `reg 36(17) the sum of tPx / (1 + i)^t from year t on` rest yield (t PLUS 1)

-- src:653 | (17) The weekly amount shall be calculated in accordance with the following formula, according to the claimant’s age on the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable:
-- src:654 | A / B
-- src:655 | where
-- src:656 | A is the lump sum payment; and
-- src:657 | B is the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week starting from the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable and payable for the claimant’s lifetime, as calculated each year in accordance with the following formula and effective on January 1 of the year following its calculation:
-- src:658 | B = [Σt = 0 to infinity of (tPx/ (1+ i)t) – 0.5] × 52
-- src:659 | where
-- src:660 | tPx is the probability that the claimant will survive for “t” years from the claimant’s age “x” using the latest Canadian mortality rates used in the valuation of the Canada Pension Plan prorated in equal parts between males and females,
-- src:661 | i is the annualized long-term Government of Canada benchmark bond yields averaged over the 12-month period beginning on the September 1 and ending on the August 30 before the January 1 on which the estimated actuarial present values are effective, expressed as a percentage and rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage, and
-- src:662 | t is the number of years that the claimant survives according to the claimant’s age for which the probablity of survival is estimated by tPx.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(17) (src:653-662)
GIVEN `the probabilities tPx that the claimant survives t years, for t = 0, 1, 2 and so on` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the annualized long-term Government of Canada benchmark bond yield i, as a rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(17) B, the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week for the claimant's lifetime` IS
    ((`reg 36(17) the sum of tPx / (1 + i)^t from year t on` `the probabilities tPx that the claimant survives t years, for t = 0, 1, 2 and so on` (`reg 36(17) the yield i rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage` `the annualized long-term Government of Canada benchmark bond yield i, as a rate`) 0) MINUS 0.5) TIMES 52

-- src:653 | (17) The weekly amount shall be calculated in accordance with the following formula, according to the claimant’s age on the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable:
-- src:654 | A / B
-- src:655 | where
-- src:656 | A is the lump sum payment; and
-- src:657 | B is the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week starting from the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable and payable for the claimant’s lifetime, as calculated each year in accordance with the following formula and effective on January 1 of the year following its calculation:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(17) (src:653-657)
GIVEN `the lump sum payment A` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the estimated actuarial present value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 36(17) the weekly amount A / B` IS
    IF `B, the estimated actuarial present value` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the lump sum payment A` DIVIDED BY `B, the estimated actuarial present value`)

-- (18) Earnings under a government re-employment program that supplement earnings from a contract of
-- employment go to the period for which they are payable.
-- src:663 | (18) Earnings that are payable to a claimant under a government program intended to encourage re-employment and that are payable to the claimant as a supplement to earnings arising from a contract of employment shall be allocated to the period for which they are payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(18) (src:663)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(18) supplements under a government program intended to encourage re-employment` IS
    IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: payable under a government program intended to encourage re-employment, as a supplement to earnings arising from a contract of employment` facts
    THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the period for which the earnings are payable`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (19) Earnings to which none of (1) to (18) apply: (a) from the performance of services, to the period in which
-- the services are performed; (b) from a transaction, to the week in which the transaction occurs. The case
-- of earnings that are neither is not covered: NOTHING. "none of subsections (1) to (18) apply" is taken as
-- "none of the manners of (2) to (18) applies" (subsection (1) is the general rule); `others` is the list of
-- the manners that those subsections gave.
-- src:664 | (19) Where a claimant has earnings to which none of subsections (1) to (18) apply, those earnings shall be allocated
-- src:665 | (a) if they arise from the performance of services, to the period in which the services are performed; and
-- src:666 | (b) if they arise from a transaction, to the week in which the transaction occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(19) (src:664-666)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
      `the manners that subsections (2) to (18) gave` IS A LIST OF `er3 Manner of allocation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36(19) earnings to which none of subsections (1) to (18) apply` IS
    IF NOT (null `the manners that subsections (2) to (18) gave`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from the performance of services` facts
         THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the period in which the services were performed`
         ELSE IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction` facts
              THEN JUST `er3 manner: to the week in which the transaction occurs`
              ELSE NOTHING

-- src:666 | (b) if they arise from a transaction, to the week in which the transaction occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(19)(b) (src:666)
GIVEN `the day on which the transaction occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `reg 36(19)(b) the week to which earnings from a transaction are allocated` IS
    `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the transaction occurs`

§ `Section 36 as a whole -- which manner governs`

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
GIVETH A LIST OF `er3 Manner of allocation`
`reg 36 a manner as a list` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST x THEN LIST x

-- The manners that apply to earnings, in this order: not allocated (2); the specific kinds first, the more
-- general later: (11) awards, (9) lay-off, (8) vacation pay, (12) listed payments, (13) holidays, (14) and (15)
-- pension moneys, (18) re-employment supplements, (7) farming, (6.1) transactions, (6.2) neither, (6) services
-- by self-employed or commission earners, (4) services under a contract, (5) no services; then (19) only if none
-- of the rest applied. The text states no priority; the order is the encoding's (fork F3). The list lets a
-- caller see every manner that applies and not only the first.
-- src:609 | (2) For the purposes of this section, the earnings of a claimant shall not be allocated to weeks during which they did not constitute earnings or were not taken into account as earnings under section 35.
-- src:610 | (3) Where the period for which earnings of a claimant are payable does not coincide with a week, the earnings shall be allocated to any week that is wholly or partly in the period in the proportion that the number of days worked in the week bears to the number of days worked in the period.
-- src:611 | (4) Earnings that are payable to a claimant under a contract of employment for the performance of services shall be allocated to the period in which the services were performed.
-- src:612 | (5) Earnings that are payable to a claimant under a contract of employment without the performance of services or payable by an employer to a claimant in consideration of the claimant returning to or beginning work shall be allocated to the period for which they are payable.
-- src:613 | (6) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that arise from the performance of services shall be allocated to the weeks in which those services are performed.
-- src:614 | (6.1) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that arise from a transaction shall be allocated
-- src:615 | (a) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is greater than the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the weeks in which the work that gave rise to the transaction was performed, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks or, if no such work was performed, to the week in which the transaction occurred; or
-- src:616 | (b) if the aggregate amount of earnings that arise from a transaction occurring in a week is less than or equal to the maximum yearly insurable earnings referred to in section 4 of the Act divided by 52, to the week in which the transaction occurred or, if the claimant demonstrates that the work that gave rise to the transaction occurred in more than one week, to the weeks in which the earnings were earned, in a manner that is proportional to the amount of work that was performed during each of those weeks.
-- src:617 | (6.2) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed, or the earnings of a claimant that are from participation in profits or commissions, that do not arise from the performance of services or from a transaction shall be allocated equally to each week falling within the period in which the earnings were earned.
-- src:618 | (7) The earnings of a claimant who is self-employed in farming shall be allocated
-- src:619 | (a) if they arose from a transaction, in accordance with subsection (6.1); and
-- src:620 | (b) if they were received in the form of a subsidy, to the week in which the subsidy was paid.
-- src:621 | (8) Where vacation pay is paid or payable to a claimant for a reason other than a lay-off or separation from an employment, it shall be allocated as follows:
-- src:622 | (a) where the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods, it shall be allocated
-- src:623 | (i) to a number of weeks that begins with the first week and ends not later than the last week of the vacation period or periods, and
-- src:624 | (ii) in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each consecutive week, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment; and
-- src:625 | (b) in any other case, the vacation pay shall, when paid, be allocated
-- src:626 | (i) to a number of weeks that begins with the first week for which it is payable, and
-- src:627 | (ii) in such a manner that, for each week except the last, the amount allocated under this subsection is equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
-- src:628 | (9) Subject to subsections (10) to (11), all earnings paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment shall, regardless of the period in respect of which the earnings are purported to be paid or payable, be allocated to a number of weeks that begins with the week of the lay-off or separation in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each consecutive week except the last, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
-- src:629 | (10) Subject to subsection (11), where earnings are paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment subsequent to an allocation under subsection (9) in respect of that lay-off or separation, the subsequent earnings shall be added to the earnings that were allocated and, regardless of the period in respect of which the subsequent earnings are purported to be paid or payable, a revised allocation shall be made in accordance with subsection (9) on the basis of that total.
-- src:630 | (10.1) The allocation of the earnings paid or payable to a claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment made in accordance with subsection (9) does not apply if
-- src:631 | (a) the claimant’s benefit period begins in the period beginning on January 25, 2009 and ending on May 29, 2010;
-- src:632 | (b) the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium in at least seven of the 10 years before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period;
-- src:633 | (c) the Commission paid the claimant less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period; and
-- src:634 | (d) during the period in which the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant’s lay-off or separation from an employment are allocated in accordance with subsection (9) or, if the earnings are allocated to five weeks or less, during that period of allocation or within six weeks following the notification of the allocation, the claimant is referred by the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act, to a course or program of instruction or training
-- src:635 | (i) that is full-time,
-- src:636 | (ii) that has a duration of at least 10 weeks or that costs at least $5,000 or 80% of the earnings paid or payable by reason of the claimant’s lay-off or separation from employment,
-- src:637 | (iii) for which the claimant assumes the entire cost, and
-- src:638 | (iv) that begins during one of the 52 weeks following the beginning of the claimant’s benefit period.
-- src:639 | (10.2) If any of the conditions under which the Commission may terminate the claimant’s referral under paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act exists, the earnings paid or payable to the claimant by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment shall be re-allocated under subsection (9).
-- src:640 | (11) Where earnings are paid or payable in respect of an employment pursuant to a labour arbitration award or the judgment of a tribunal, or as a settlement of an issue that might otherwise have been determined by a labour arbitration award or the judgment of a tribunal, and the earnings are awarded in respect of specific weeks as a result of a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted, the earnings shall be allocated to a number of consecutive weeks, beginning with the first week in respect of which the earnings are awarded, in such a manner that the total earnings of the claimant from that employment are, in each week except the last week, equal to the claimant’s normal weekly earnings from that employment.
-- src:641 | (12) The following payments shall be allocated to the weeks in respect of which the payments are paid or payable:
-- src:642 | (a) payments in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act;
-- src:643 | (b) payments under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan;
-- src:644 | (c) payments referred to in paragraphs 35(2)(d) and (f);
-- src:645 | (d) workers’ compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers’ compensation payments;
-- src:646 | (e) payments in respect of the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act;
-- src:647 | (f) payments in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child; and
-- src:648 | (g) payments in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult.
-- src:649 | (13) A payment paid or payable to a claimant in respect of a holiday or non-working day that is observed as such by law, custom or agreement, or a holiday or non-working day immediately preceding or following a holiday or non-working day that occurs at the establishment of the employer or former employer from whom the claimant receives that payment, shall be allocated to the week in which that day occurs.
-- src:650 | (14) The moneys referred to in paragraph 35(2)(e) that are paid or payable to a claimant on a periodic basis shall be allocated to the period for which they are paid or payable.
-- src:651 | (15) The moneys referred to in paragraph 35(2)(e) that are paid or payable to a claimant in a lump sum shall be allocated beginning with the first week that those moneys are paid or payable to the claimant in such a manner that those moneys are equal in each week to the weekly amount, calculated in accordance with subsection (17), to which the claimant would have been entitled if the lump sum payment had been paid as an annuity.
-- src:652 | (16) The moneys allocated in accordance with subsection (14) or (15) shall not be taken into account in the allocation of other earnings under this section.
-- src:653 | (17) The weekly amount shall be calculated in accordance with the following formula, according to the claimant’s age on the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable:
-- src:654 | A / B
-- src:655 | where
-- src:656 | A is the lump sum payment; and
-- src:657 | B is the estimated actuarial present value of $1 payable at the beginning of every week starting from the day on which the lump sum payment is paid or payable and payable for the claimant’s lifetime, as calculated each year in accordance with the following formula and effective on January 1 of the year following its calculation:
-- src:658 | B = [Σt = 0 to infinity of (tPx/ (1+ i)t) – 0.5] × 52
-- src:659 | where
-- src:660 | tPx is the probability that the claimant will survive for “t” years from the claimant’s age “x” using the latest Canadian mortality rates used in the valuation of the Canada Pension Plan prorated in equal parts between males and females,
-- src:661 | i is the annualized long-term Government of Canada benchmark bond yields averaged over the 12-month period beginning on the September 1 and ending on the August 30 before the January 1 on which the estimated actuarial present values are effective, expressed as a percentage and rounded to the nearest one tenth of a percentage, and
-- src:662 | t is the number of years that the claimant survives according to the claimant’s age for which the probablity of survival is estimated by tPx.
-- src:663 | (18) Earnings that are payable to a claimant under a government program intended to encourage re-employment and that are payable to the claimant as a supplement to earnings arising from a contract of employment shall be allocated to the period for which they are payable.
-- src:664 | (19) Where a claimant has earnings to which none of subsections (1) to (18) apply, those earnings shall be allocated
-- src:665 | (a) if they arise from the performance of services, to the period in which the services are performed; and
-- src:666 | (b) if they arise from a transaction, to the week in which the transaction occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 36(2) to (19) (src:609-666)
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A LIST OF `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36 the manners of allocation that apply` IS
    LET before19 MEANS concat (map `reg 36 a manner as a list` (LIST
            (IF `reg 36 the fact holds of the earnings` `er3 earnings: they did not constitute earnings, or were not taken into account as earnings, under section 35` facts
             THEN JUST `er3 manner: not allocated to any week` ELSE NOTHING),
            `reg 36(11) earnings awarded for specific weeks following a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted` facts,
            `reg 36(9) earnings paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment` facts,
            `reg 36(8) vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation` facts,
            `reg 36(12) payments allocated to the weeks in respect of which they are paid or payable` facts,
            `reg 36(13) a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day` facts,
            `reg 36(14) pension moneys paid or payable on a periodic basis` facts,
            `reg 36(15) pension moneys paid or payable in a lump sum` facts,
            `reg 36(18) supplements under a government program intended to encourage re-employment` facts,
            `reg 36(7) earnings of a claimant who is self-employed in farming` facts,
            `reg 36(6.1) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from a transaction` facts,
            `reg 36(6.2) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from neither services nor a transaction` facts,
            `reg 36(6) self-employed or profits or commissions earnings that arise from the performance of services` facts,
            `reg 36(4) earnings payable under a contract of employment for the performance of services` facts,
            `reg 36(5) earnings payable without the performance of services or to induce a return to or the beginning of work` facts))
    IN append before19 (`reg 36 a manner as a list` (`reg 36(19) earnings to which none of subsections (1) to (18) apply` facts before19))

-- The manner that governs: the first on that list; none: not covered, NOTHING.
GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `reg 36 the manner of allocation that governs` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 36 the manners of allocation that apply` facts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST m
